    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-upside plays at the corner infield spots. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.26) serve as our top-tier options, both benefiting significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) despite facing a moderate threat in McClanahan. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a traditional platoon disadvantage, his raw output remains elite; conversely, **Coby Mayo** maximizes the park and platoon alignment, making him our strongest play of the day. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) rounds out our top three, maintaining steady production against the lefty Weathers, where his dynamic platoon advantage helps offset the challenge of an otherwise solid arm.\n\nBeyond our core, we are leaning heavily into specific situational advantages to maintain our edge in the standings. **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) remains a primary focus; while our model accounts for a slight drop due to his hold on stolen base opportunities, his favorable matchup against Kremer and a high-leverage lineup spot make him a near-must-start. We continue to monitor the status of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung**, all of whom remain on the IL, further complicating our depth. Our most difficult bench decision was choosing between **Heliot Ramos** (45.34) and **Miguel Vargas** (45.54); despite **Miguel Vargas** posting a marginally higher efficiency score, the defensive versatility and specific speed-profile advantages of **Heliot Ramos** kept him in the active lineup to protect our stolen base metrics, which remain the scarcest category for the Waves. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the Cease matchup for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**; while their scores are boosted by positive park factors, Cease remains a high-strikeout threat who could dampen our daily efficiency. We are also keeping an eye on **Nasim Nunez**, whose score (45.85) remains on the lower end of our starting threshold due to his placement in the #8 spot. As we navigate the remainder of the season, the health of our bench depth\u2014including **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**\u2014will be vital should we need to pivot from current starters facing these late-August elite arms.",
